or if it just has a low 9-volt battery.

1296
01:01:23,720 --> 01:01:27,600
You need the evidence to know whether to evacuate your family or just go to the hardware store.

1297
01:01:27,600 --> 01:01:28,160
Exactly.

1298
01:01:28,380 --> 01:01:34,260
A passport application rejected with no reason attached, just stamped no, leaves you completely stuck.

1299
01:01:34,500 --> 01:01:36,860
You need to know why it was rejected to fix it.

1300
01:01:36,860 --> 01:01:39,620
And this is about the concept of boundary propagation.

1301
01:01:39,820 --> 01:01:40,100
Okay.

1302
01:01:40,420 --> 01:01:54,600
When a boundary in a system encounters a failure, swallowing the error like mapping a highly specific database timeout or a corrupted file error down to a generic failed string destroys the boundary's knowledge.

1303
01:01:54,680 --> 01:01:55,600
It hides the truth.

1304
01:01:55,600 --> 01:01:57,100
It throws away the evidence.

1305
01:01:57,100 --> 01:02:02,120
It forces the caller higher up the chain to blindly guess what went wrong.

1306
01:02:02,860 --> 01:02:10,580
A robust system should propagate the exact evidence of failure so that the caller can make a logically informed decision about how to actually recover.

1307
01:02:10,580 --> 01:02:16,460
It's about preserving the absolute truth of the system at every single level of the stack.

1308
01:02:17,040 --> 01:02:18,760
Don't swallow the error with a catch-all.

1309
01:02:19,080 --> 01:02:21,220
Don't use mannequins for empty seats.

1310
01:02:21,580 --> 01:02:23,980
Don't pretend a milk frother can knead dough.

1311
01:02:24,560 --> 01:02:28,460
And don't let two people edit a book at the same time without telling each other.

1312
01:02:28,740 --> 01:02:34,540
When you lay it out sequentially like that, you can see the grand unifying theory of the entire manuscript.

1313
01:02:34,720 --> 01:02:35,360
It's all connected.

1314
01:02:35,360 --> 01:02:46,060
Rusts, strict rules, unique authority, explicit state spaces, exhaustive pattern matching, precise trait bounds, honest partiality.

1315
01:02:46,160 --> 01:02:48,520
None of these are separate arbitrary annoyances.

1316
01:02:48,780 --> 01:02:49,020
No.

1317
01:02:49,240 --> 01:02:55,820
They are all just different facets of the exact same underlying principle, bounding the context required for correct reasoning.

1318
01:02:55,880 --> 01:02:57,120
It's breathtaking, honestly.

1319
01:02:57,120 --> 01:03:07,020
We went from two cooks making a pound cake to a mechanic fixing a car to the strict mathematical rules of unique authority, product, and some state spaces and honest boundaries.

1320
01:03:07,180 --> 01:03:07,620
It's a journey.

1321
01:03:07,760 --> 01:03:11,660
It completely changes how you look at constraints in any system, not just code.

1322
01:03:12,000 --> 01:03:13,220
They aren't there to slow you down.

1323
01:03:13,340 --> 01:03:14,960
The bouncer isn't there to ruin your night.

1324
01:03:15,320 --> 01:03:18,580
They are there to make the system actually align with physical reality.

1325
01:03:18,940 --> 01:03:19,700
They are generative.

1326
01:03:19,800 --> 01:03:19,980
Yeah.

1327
01:03:19,980 --> 01:03:30,380
By restricting the chaos, by completely eliminating action at a distance, they allow you to build towering, complex structures of logic that you can actually fundamentally trust.

1328
